CYCLE=0
IDEA=$'Graceful termination — give a healthy teammate a final turn to write memory before it is killed.\n\n**Goal**\n\nWhen the coordinator (or shutdown) terminates a *healthy* claude-crew teammate, give that\nteammate one final turn to distill anything worth saving into its project-scoped memory — per\nthe memory guidance ALREADY injected into its system prompt at spawn — before the broker\ntombstones it. A graceful termination, replacing today\'s immediate hard kill.\n\n**Problem (current behavior)**\n\nTermination does NO memory distillation today. broker._tombstone_teammate (the shared\nkill+death path, claude_crew/broker.py:361-557) does: end-turn, snapshot telemetry into the\ntombstone, bounce in-flight + queued envelopes, close open tools, emit a lifecycle event,\ndetached shutdown(). It never calls build_memory_section / memory_dir / ensure_write_tool.\nThe memory feature (multi-scope-agent-memory) is entirely SPAWN-SIDE and self-directed: at\nSdkTeammate.__init__ the teammate gets the Write tool (ensure_write_tool) plus a memory\naddendum in its system prompt (build_memory_section), and writes memory itself mid-session if\nit chooses. Kill it before it self-distills and that conversation\'s lessons are lost.\n\nAlso: doc/sdk-teammate-wiring.md line 109 currently claims "Auto-distilled at kill_teammate exit" —\nthis is FALSE today. Fix that line as part of this feature (doc-sync).\n\n**Locked design decisions (user-confirmed)**\n\n1. DEFAULT-ON, auto-skip when no memory surface. The flush runs whenever the teammate has the\n   Write tool AND a memory scope; auto-skipped (zero cost, immediate tombstone) for memory-less\n   teammates. A graceful=False parameter on the kill path forces an immediate hard kill.\n2. 90s flush budget. Matches the established hang-detection budget in this codebase. On timeout,\n   fall through to the existing hard tombstone (partial memory writes are fine — Write is\n   incremental and the file persists).\n3. INTERRUPT the in-flight turn and flush immediately. The in-flight turn\'s result is already\n   discarded on kill today (bounced as teammate_dead), so do not wait for it to finish.\n4. shutdown_all flushes too — PARALLEL, under ONE shared 90s deadline (not N x 90s sequential).\n\n**Architecture findings (load-bearing — verified against the code)**\n\n- The flush MUST run on the SAME ClaudeSDKClient session the teammate has been using (_run\n  holds it in its async-with ClaudeSDKClient(...) block, sdk_teammate.py:1329). A fresh\n  session has no conversation to distill from. Therefore the flush turn must execute INSIDE the\n  teammate\'s own _run loop task (the single owner of client), NOT in the broker\'s task.\n- _handle_one_turn (sdk_teammate.py:1356) already implements the exact sequence a flush needs:\n  client.query(...) then a bounded _collect_response_text drain, and on backstop-timeout an\n  client.interrupt() -> bounded-grace -> re-drain ladder (sdk_teammate.py:1376-1404). The\n  flush reuses this proven machinery; interrupt is not a new primitive here.\n- Idle vs busy unify under one termination signal:\n    - IDLE (teammate blocked on inbox.get()): inject a flush sentinel to break the wait, run the\n      flush turn, then exit the loop.\n    - BUSY (inside _handle_one_turn): client.interrupt() breaks the in-flight drain; the turn\n      handler observes the termination signal and runs the flush turn inline (same task, same\n      client), then exits.\n- Proposed control flow: broker.kill_teammate(graceful=True) ->\n  await teammate.begin_graceful_termination(timeout=90) (stores/uses the client ref, sets a\n  _terminating flag, interrupts the in-flight turn or enqueues the flush sentinel, awaits a\n  _flush_complete event bounded by the timeout) -> THEN the existing _tombstone_teammate runs\n  unchanged. Tombstone ordering invariants (D2 tombstone-before-pop, idempotency) are preserved\n  because the flush happens BEFORE tombstone step 1.\n- New intermediate teammate state during the flush window: the teammate is no longer accepting\n  normal work but is not yet tombstoned. New sends arriving during the window should bounce\n  (teammate-already-dead semantics) so the flush turn is not interleaved with real traffic.\n\n**Flush prompt**\n\nA synthetic final turn that LEANS ON the already-injected memory guidance — do NOT re-explain the\nsave rules. Approximately: "You are about to be terminated. Per your memory instructions, persist\nanything worth saving now using the Write tool, then stop. Do nothing else." Bounded by 90s.\n\n**Edge cases (must be specified + tested)**\n\n- No memory surface (no Write tool / no scope) -> skip flush, immediate tombstone (decision 1).\n- graceful=False -> skip flush, immediate hard kill.\n- DEATH detection (broker._handle_teammate_death) -> NEVER flush; the subprocess is already gone.\n  Graceful applies only to explicit kill of a live, healthy teammate.\n- Flush turn hangs -> 90s timeout -> proceed to hard tombstone. (If client.interrupt() itself\n  hangs, the existing _death_suspected wedge path applies.)\n- Flush turn raises an SDK error -> log, proceed to tombstone (don\'t block teardown).\n- Interrupt unsupported / raises -> graceful-degrade to hard kill.\n- Double kill -> idempotent (already-dead error), as today.\n- StubTeammate needs a no-op / simple flush implementation so non-SDK tests can exercise the\n  broker orchestration without the SDK.\n\n**Validation strategy (per repo standards — two layers, happy + sad, plus gated live)**\n\n- IMPLEMENTATION layer: begin_graceful_termination / the flush turn — stub-level unit tests for\n  the state transitions and the idle-sentinel vs busy-interrupt branch; PLUS a gated live test\n  (CLAUDE_CREW_LIVE_TESTS=1) proving a real SDK teammate actually writes a memory file when flushed.\n- INTEGRATION layer (broker): kill_teammate(graceful=True) -> flush turn ran -> memory written;\n  auto-skip path (no Write -> no flush, immediate tombstone); graceful=False -> immediate;\n  timeout path (flush hangs -> hard kill after budget, telemetry tombstone intact); shutdown_all\n  parallel flush under one shared deadline.\n- Happy AND sad paths at BOTH layers.\n- Bound any open-ended async-iterator drains in tests with asyncio.wait_for (repo convention).\n- RUN THE FULL SUITE (uv run pytest) for the validation gate, not a keyword-filtered subset —\n  this mutates the termination path that many suites assert on (CLAUDE.md: validate the whole\n  suite when changing widely-consumed behavior). Stub-mode is the default; live tests stay gated.\n\n**Surfaces likely touched (pointers for the planner to read)**\n\n- claude_crew/broker.py — kill_teammate (:597), _tombstone_teammate (:361), shutdown_all (:607),\n  _handle_teammate_death (:589). New pre-tombstone flush step; graceful parameter; intermediate\n  terminating-state bookkeeping.\n- claude_crew/sdk_teammate.py — _run (:1186), _handle_one_turn (:1356), interrupt ladder\n  (:1376-1404), shutdown (:1602). Client-ref storage, _terminating/_flush_complete, flush turn,\n  sentinel handling, begin_graceful_termination.\n- claude_crew/teammate.py — abstract base: a begin_graceful_termination hook + StubTeammate flush.\n- claude_crew/teammate_memory.py — REUSE as-is (read/inject side). Do NOT build a new distillation\n  engine; the teammate distills itself via its injected guidance + the Write tool.\n- claude_crew/server.py — kill_teammate MCP tool (:456 / :484) gains a graceful (and possibly\n  flush_timeout) argument threaded to broker.kill_teammate.\n- doc/sdk-teammate-wiring.md line 109 — fix the false "auto-distilled at kill" claim.\n\n**Non-goals / out of scope**\n\n- No memory distillation on unexpected DEATH (process already gone — can\'t flush).\n- No new summarization/distillation engine — reuse the existing injected-guidance + Write-tool\n  self-distill mechanism.\n- No change to the spawn-side memory injection (multi-scope-agent-memory) — that stays as is.\n- No peer-to-peer or autonomous behavior — the coordinator/shutdown still owns the kill decision.\n\n**Reference**\n\nA fuller design brief lives in the MAIN repo at\n/home/jerome/dev/claude-crew/doc/ideas/graceful-termination-memory-flush.md (untracked; not in\nthis worktree). Same content as above; this idea.txt is authoritative for the slice.'
